teleddns (0.3.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add resync_interval (default 24h): re-send the DDNS update when nothing
    has been pushed for that long, repairing a record lost by the server.
    The deadline is measured from the last successful update, and every
    resync re-reads the addresses from the kernel before reporting them.
  * Add redump_interval (default 15m): rebuild the address table from a full
    kernel dump, reconciling state left stale by a dropped netlink message.
  * Retry failed updates with exponential backoff, per address family: 30s
    after the first failure, doubling to 15m, reset on success. Previously a
    failed update was retried every 31s indefinitely.
  * Add debian/copyright; the package shipped without license information.
  * Use "teleddns" as the only project name in output and documentation.

 -- Tomas Hlavacek <tmshlvck@gmail.com>  Fri, 10 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0000

teleddns (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Port to Go; drop-in replacement for the Rust package.
  * Build with the Go toolchain via debhelper instead of cargo-deb/zigbuild.
  * Build a static binary with CGO disabled; the Go internal linker
    cross-compiles to every architecture with no C toolchain.
  * No OpenSSL dependency (Go's TLS is pure Go).
  * Ship /var/lib/teleddns for the persisted push state; removed on purge.

 -- Tomas Hlavacek <tmshlvck@gmail.com>  Sun, 28 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
